        "original_id": "f3d8bbdf-b3e8-5b70-b7fd-4dfa44c016a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johan Henrik Deuntzer\n- Organizations: Venstre, Danish Social Liberal Party, Venstre Reform Party\n- Places: Denmark\n- Roles: Council President\n- Events: 1901 Danish Folketing election\n- Governments: Cabinet of Deuntzer\n\nFacts:\n- Johan Henrik Deuntzer was born on 20 May 1845 and died on 16 November 1918.\n- After the 1901 Danish Folketing election, Council President Johan Henrik Deuntzer of the Venstre Reform Party became the leader of Denmark's first liberal government.\n- Johan Henrik Deuntzer was a Danish politician and a member of the Liberal party Venstre until 1905, when he joined the Danish Social Liberal Party.\n- The Danish Social Liberal Party, also called Radikale Venstre or Radical Left, is a social-liberal political party in Denmark.",
